1
00:00:02,054 --> 00:00:05,057
- [wind blowing]
- [suspenseful music playing]

2
00:00:19,947 --> 00:00:21,949
[suspenseful music continues]

3
00:00:37,882 --> 00:00:39,884
- [blender whirring]
- [chiming]

4
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:10,122
{\an8}[gulping]

5
00:01:12,750 --> 00:01:13,959
{\an8}[sighs contentedly]

6
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,672
{\an8}No wonder the January report was so late.

7
00:01:19,965 --> 00:01:21,467
{\an8}Unbelievable.

8
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:24,845
{\an8}A 17-year-old wolf
with a whole life ahead of him

9
00:01:25,596 --> 00:01:28,349
eats the leg of his friend, a deer.

10
00:01:29,433 --> 00:01:32,061
How many more of these cases
do I have to see?

11
00:01:33,604 --> 00:01:34,522
Oh, hang on.

12
00:01:35,105 --> 00:01:36,148
{\an8}REPORT
NAME: LEGOSHI

13
00:01:36,232 --> 00:01:39,360
{\an8}"The objective, which was mutually
agreed upon with the victim,

14
00:01:40,194 --> 00:01:43,114
{\an8}was to bring a devourer to justice"?

15
00:01:44,448 --> 00:01:45,282
{\an8}Really?

16
00:01:46,534 --> 00:01:49,829
{\an8}So we're fighting fire with fire,
are we, boys?

17
00:01:49,912 --> 00:01:51,455
{\an8}DISCHARGED

18
00:01:51,539 --> 00:01:52,498
{\an8}Interesting.

19
00:01:53,624 --> 00:01:56,377
{\an8}But still despicable.

20
00:01:57,044 --> 00:01:58,045
TOP SECRET

21
00:01:58,129 --> 00:02:02,299
{\an8}He may have agreed to it,
but I sure as hell do not.

22
00:02:07,471 --> 00:02:09,807
As the Beastar of this world,

23
00:02:11,100 --> 00:02:12,768
I can't let it go.

24
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:39,962
AN ITCHY COLLAR

25
00:02:40,045 --> 00:02:42,047
[suspenseful music playing]

26
00:02:51,974 --> 00:02:53,976
[Legoshi groaning in agony]

27
00:02:58,022 --> 00:03:01,233
BEAST APARTMENTS

28
00:03:01,317 --> 00:03:04,862
[Legoshi groaning in agony]

29
00:03:06,947 --> 00:03:09,617
[Legoshi groaning, whimpering]

30
00:03:15,539 --> 00:03:18,542
- [Legoshi groaning, whimpering]
- [objects clattering]

31
00:03:23,255 --> 00:03:26,258
[Legoshi continues groaning]

32
00:03:31,138 --> 00:03:34,600
- [Legoshi groaning, panting]
- [objects thudding]

33
00:03:39,063 --> 00:03:40,481
[Legoshi shouts]

34
00:03:42,358 --> 00:03:45,486
[Legoshi groaning, whimpering]

35
00:03:59,208 --> 00:04:00,042
[grunts]

36
00:04:00,125 --> 00:04:03,420
[panting, straining]

37
00:04:05,005 --> 00:04:07,049
- [Louis] <i>I want you to eat me.</i>
- [gasps]

38
00:04:08,801 --> 00:04:10,552
[Legoshi] <i>I swore
I'd never eat meat again.</i>

39
00:04:11,553 --> 00:04:12,638
<i>I made a vow.</i>

40
00:04:12,721 --> 00:04:15,849
- [Saiga] <i>Choose your favorite finger.</i>
- [Legoshi] <i>But the taste...</i>

41
00:04:15,933 --> 00:04:17,268
<i>The texture.</i>

42
00:04:17,351 --> 00:04:19,979
- [Bill] <i>Do you want a bite? Rabbit blood.</i>
- [Legoshi] <i>The flavor...</i>

43
00:04:20,062 --> 00:04:21,480
<i>The moisture.</i>

44
00:04:21,563 --> 00:04:23,065
[pants, grunts]

45
00:04:24,275 --> 00:04:25,442
<i>So warm.</i>

46
00:04:26,986 --> 00:04:27,987
<i>I'm powerless,</i>

47
00:04:29,405 --> 00:04:30,489
<i>and sorrowful...</i>

48
00:04:32,032 --> 00:04:34,660
[Black Legoshi] <i>You feel joy
from the bottom of your heart.</i>

49
00:04:34,743 --> 00:04:36,745
[Gohin] <i>No matter how much
you struggle against it,</i>

50
00:04:36,829 --> 00:04:39,915
<i>your true nature is that of
a brutal, vicious carnivore.</i>

51
00:04:39,999 --> 00:04:44,253
[Legoshi] <i>I was always...
struggling with my own blood.</i>

52
00:04:47,881 --> 00:04:52,720
<i>I want to make sure this world is a place
where Haru can live in peace.</i>

53
00:04:52,803 --> 00:04:53,637
[gasps softly]

54
00:04:54,805 --> 00:04:55,639
<i>And yet...</i>

55
00:04:55,723 --> 00:04:56,807
[growls softly]

56
00:04:58,809 --> 00:05:03,897
<i>...the blood that flows through these veins...
still wants for living flesh!</i>

57
00:05:03,981 --> 00:05:06,984
[screaming in agony]

58
00:05:09,153 --> 00:05:11,155
[whimpers]

59
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:16,243
[groaning in agony]

60
00:05:20,205 --> 00:05:21,415
[Seven sighs in annoyance]

61
00:05:22,499 --> 00:05:25,210
- [Legoshi continues groaning]
- [Seven sighs]

62
00:05:25,961 --> 00:05:29,715
<i>Ugh! So loud!
Every night, it's the same thing!</i>

63
00:05:29,798 --> 00:05:31,592
<i>And I have work in the morning!</i>

64
00:05:31,675 --> 00:05:34,470
[Legoshi continues groaning]

65
00:05:37,097 --> 00:05:38,891
[Seven] <i>What kind of person
acts like this?</i>

66
00:05:38,974 --> 00:05:41,977
<i>Not even a "Hello, neighbor"
when he moved in.</i>

67
00:05:42,061 --> 00:05:43,937
<i>Well, I got something to say to him!</i>

68
00:05:48,067 --> 00:05:48,984
[gasps]

69
00:05:50,861 --> 00:05:52,571
<i>- A wolf...</i>
- [Legoshi grunts softly]

70
00:05:53,739 --> 00:05:55,199
[Seven] <i>What do I say?</i>

71
00:05:55,282 --> 00:05:57,618
<i>Complaining might not be
the best way to start.</i>

72
00:05:57,701 --> 00:05:59,203
- [water flowing]
- [Seven sighs]

73
00:06:00,037 --> 00:06:02,831
[Legoshi panting]

74
00:06:06,001 --> 00:06:08,170
Uh, excuse me, sir?

75
00:06:10,547 --> 00:06:11,673
- Huh?
- [exclaims]

76
00:06:12,883 --> 00:06:16,220
Good evening. I'm Seven,
and I live in the room next door.

77
00:06:16,929 --> 00:06:18,305
- It's a pleasure--
- [Legoshi gasps]

78
00:06:18,388 --> 00:06:20,015
- [Seven gasps]
- [Legoshi exhales]

79
00:06:25,354 --> 00:06:26,522
<i>What's with him?</i>

80
00:06:26,605 --> 00:06:28,649
<i>That's a rather rude way to treat people.</i>

81
00:06:28,732 --> 00:06:30,025
<i>Unbelievable!</i>

82
00:06:32,152 --> 00:06:34,822
[Legoshi] <i>Sorry about that, neighbor.</i>

83
00:06:37,241 --> 00:06:39,243
[train chugging]

84
00:06:41,453 --> 00:06:43,872
[female dog grunting in distance]

85
00:06:50,879 --> 00:06:52,798
[grunting, straining]

86
00:06:56,176 --> 00:06:59,054
[Gohin] <i>Hmm? No meat response.</i>

87
00:06:59,930 --> 00:07:03,767
[inhales deeply] <i>If that dog really
isn't eating meat,</i>

88
00:07:03,851 --> 00:07:08,188
<i>then these symptoms are a bit unusual.</i>

89
00:07:10,691 --> 00:07:13,152
<i>If it's not meat intoxication...</i>

90
00:07:13,819 --> 00:07:14,653
[knock on door]

91
00:07:15,863 --> 00:07:17,865
[Legoshi] It's me, I have your food!

92
00:07:17,948 --> 00:07:18,991
Finally!

93
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:20,868
Come on in, kid.

94
00:07:23,704 --> 00:07:24,913
Put it anywhere.

95
00:07:28,792 --> 00:07:30,252
[Legoshi grunts softly]

96
00:07:30,335 --> 00:07:33,755
[Legoshi] Straight-from-the-pot udon
with bamboo leaf topping.

97
00:07:33,839 --> 00:07:36,258
Sorry for the wait. That's 500.

98
00:07:36,341 --> 00:07:39,011
Nice uniform there.
You can pull off anything.

99
00:07:39,094 --> 00:07:41,722
[scoffs] At least I'm not
dressing like a girl again.

100
00:07:41,805 --> 00:07:45,434
Good. 'Cause I almost had a heart attack.
I thought my ex-wife had come back.

101
00:07:45,517 --> 00:07:46,560
[laughs]

102
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:48,061
Well, sit down.

103
00:07:50,439 --> 00:07:52,691
[gasps] What in the world are you doing?

104
00:07:52,774 --> 00:07:55,903
[chuckles nervously] No, I'd rather stand.

105
00:07:56,487 --> 00:07:59,740
- [female dog, faintly] Just one gulp.
- [Gohin slurping]

106
00:07:59,823 --> 00:08:01,575
[female dog, straining] Kines...

107
00:08:01,658 --> 00:08:06,580
So, uh, even though I had permission
to eat his leg, the truth is,

108
00:08:06,663 --> 00:08:08,957
I was prepared
to make up for it in prison.

109
00:08:09,958 --> 00:08:13,337
But then, thanks to Louis and the others
testifying for me...

110
00:08:13,420 --> 00:08:14,546
[Gohin slurping]

111
00:08:14,630 --> 00:08:17,841
...they ended up letting me go
with just a minor offense charge.

112
00:08:19,009 --> 00:08:23,555
Although, "Record of prior devouring"
will have to stay in my file.

113
00:08:23,639 --> 00:08:27,059
[Gohin] A scarred-up violent,
criminal virgin, huh? [scoffs]

114
00:08:27,809 --> 00:08:29,311
So, you're still catching meat eaters

115
00:08:29,394 --> 00:08:31,438
to bring 'em back here and treat 'em,
I take it?

116
00:08:32,564 --> 00:08:33,899
[Gohin] Hmm.

117
00:08:34,691 --> 00:08:37,027
Yeah, the situation's worse than ever.

118
00:08:37,778 --> 00:08:40,739
I don't suppose you'd want to help me
with my work again, would you?

119
00:08:40,822 --> 00:08:43,242
- [chuckles nervously]
- I can pay more than that udon place.

120
00:08:43,325 --> 00:08:46,787
Forget it, I don't want to.
The whole thing's way too shady for me.

121
00:08:46,870 --> 00:08:49,456
- What was that, you little punk?
- [Legoshi exclaims]

122
00:08:51,166 --> 00:08:54,628
Look, I just mean, I want legitimate work,
out in the open.

123
00:08:54,711 --> 00:08:59,299
I want to be a normal member of society
and lead a happy family life with Haru.

124
00:08:59,383 --> 00:09:00,425
[gulps, sighs]

125
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:04,513
- And how's that family life going?
- Huh?

126
00:09:05,222 --> 00:09:07,933
Uh, my family? I don't know--

127
00:09:08,016 --> 00:09:12,187
Look, don't answer if you don't want to.
I was just curious is all.

128
00:09:12,271 --> 00:09:13,397
[hesitates] Well...

129
00:09:14,022 --> 00:09:15,941
I don't have a mom or dad.

130
00:09:17,359 --> 00:09:18,986
I used to live with my grandpa.

131
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:21,780
[Gohin] Is your grandpa well?

132
00:09:22,364 --> 00:09:23,824
[Legoshi] You know, probably...

133
00:09:24,491 --> 00:09:26,785
[Gohin] Hmm. I see.

134
00:09:27,411 --> 00:09:28,495
[Legoshi] We, uh...

135
00:09:29,162 --> 00:09:32,332
We get along just fine and all,
but, I, uh... I haven't...

136
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:36,253
mentioned to him that I got arrested yet.

137
00:09:37,713 --> 00:09:38,922
[Gohin sighs softly]

138
00:09:41,967 --> 00:09:43,218
- Hang on a sec.
- Hmm?

139
00:09:43,302 --> 00:09:44,803
- [Gohin] Here's the drugs.
- Oh, right.

140
00:09:45,387 --> 00:09:48,015
[Gohin] Meat withdrawal symptoms
can be pretty severe

141
00:09:48,098 --> 00:09:49,641
for up to three months or so.

142
00:09:50,642 --> 00:09:52,686
- Better take them.
- [sighs] Yeah.

143
00:09:53,770 --> 00:09:55,022
I appreciate it.

144
00:09:55,772 --> 00:09:56,607
[Gohin] Sure.

145
00:09:57,691 --> 00:09:59,610
- See you later.
- Yeah. All right, then.

146
00:10:00,569 --> 00:10:02,362
[door bangs]

147
00:10:02,446 --> 00:10:03,280
Ah!

148
00:10:04,865 --> 00:10:06,575
- Legoshi!
- Uh, yeah?

149
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:09,953
"Record of prior devouring,"
was the official wording?

150
00:10:10,579 --> 00:10:11,413
Yes.

151
00:10:11,997 --> 00:10:13,123
Then I should say,

152
00:10:13,206 --> 00:10:16,126
there's one thing you won't be able to do
with that in your file.

153
00:10:16,209 --> 00:10:17,044
[Legoshi] Hmm?

154
00:10:17,127 --> 00:10:19,379
Interspecies marriage with an herbivore.

155
00:10:19,463 --> 00:10:22,049
What? I can't get married?

156
00:10:23,175 --> 00:10:24,760
No!

157
00:10:25,677 --> 00:10:31,224
Haru!

158
00:10:35,437 --> 00:10:37,189
[objects clattering]

159
00:10:37,272 --> 00:10:39,149
Oh, to be young and in love!

160
00:10:39,232 --> 00:10:40,817
[Legoshi groaning softly]

161
00:10:43,695 --> 00:10:45,030
[soft clattering]

162
00:10:47,699 --> 00:10:49,951
[Louis sighs] Ibuki.

163
00:10:50,994 --> 00:10:54,581
The king of the beasts
is supposed to be fierce and strong...

164
00:10:54,665 --> 00:10:55,916
[chuckles softly]

165
00:10:55,999 --> 00:10:58,543
...yet your rule was much like your mane.

166
00:10:58,627 --> 00:11:00,128
Beautiful and gentle.

167
00:11:01,672 --> 00:11:03,256
[gloomy guitar music playing]

168
00:11:03,340 --> 00:11:05,342
[footsteps approaching]

169
00:11:11,932 --> 00:11:14,101
How is it? The new leg, I mean.

170
00:11:14,768 --> 00:11:17,312
It was remarkably easy
to learn to walk again.

171
00:11:17,396 --> 00:11:18,563
[grunts softly]

172
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:23,610
You're quite fortunate.
It was built with the latest technology.

173
00:11:24,194 --> 00:11:26,279
I only hope it won't affect your studies.

174
00:11:29,074 --> 00:11:31,451
[grunts softly] No, sir. Thank you.

175
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:35,664
You do realize those legs of yours

176
00:11:35,747 --> 00:11:39,042
are meant to walk the path of the heir
to The Horns Conglomerate.

177
00:11:39,835 --> 00:11:42,295
They are not meant to feed
your carnivore friends.

178
00:11:43,755 --> 00:11:44,840
Yes, sir.

179
00:11:44,923 --> 00:11:48,301
I don't mind a little improvising,
but that's too far.

180
00:11:49,219 --> 00:11:51,847
You're saying I should live
according to your script?

181
00:11:52,639 --> 00:11:54,850
[Ogma chuckles] In a way.

182
00:11:55,684 --> 00:11:56,810
But more importantly,

183
00:11:57,644 --> 00:12:02,441
I want you to think for yourself,
find and fulfill your own role.

184
00:12:03,733 --> 00:12:04,568
[Louis sighs]

185
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:08,780
[Louis] <i>I thought that living
on the edges of society was the answer,</i>

186
00:12:09,865 --> 00:12:11,491
<i>but I suppose now,</i>

187
00:12:12,826 --> 00:12:16,413
<i>I have to confront
how I'm meant to live within it.</i>

188
00:12:20,709 --> 00:12:23,128
[upbeat music playing]

189
00:12:28,425 --> 00:12:31,428
[indistinct chatter]

190
00:12:41,438 --> 00:12:45,567
So I heard you went to the Black Market.
You lose your meat virginity yet?

191
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:47,194
- [chuckles]
- What kind did you get?

192
00:12:47,277 --> 00:12:48,737
It was... I think, pig.

193
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:51,239
What, you "think"?
What do you mean, you "think"?

194
00:12:51,323 --> 00:12:54,201
- Who cares what it was? I ate it.
- [student, sarcastically] Oh, yeah.

195
00:12:56,828 --> 00:13:00,248
A year ago, that conversation
never would have happened.

196
00:13:00,332 --> 00:13:01,958
- [Gon clears throat]
- [Jack] Hmm.

197
00:13:02,626 --> 00:13:04,002
CHERRYTON OPENING CEREMONY

198
00:13:04,085 --> 00:13:04,961
Welcome, all.

199
00:13:05,795 --> 00:13:09,883
As you already know,
beginning with this academic year,

200
00:13:09,966 --> 00:13:12,427
our carnivore and herbivore students

201
00:13:12,511 --> 00:13:16,014
will be split into two separate
academic tracks.

202
00:13:16,890 --> 00:13:22,229
You understand that we must, at all cost,
avoid a repeat of last year's tragedy.

203
00:13:22,312 --> 00:13:26,775
I'm sure this may seem confusing,
but as Cherryton... [continues indistinctly]

204
00:13:26,858 --> 00:13:29,569
[student 1] Maybe the classrooms
will smell better now.

205
00:13:29,653 --> 00:13:32,072
[student 2] Getting rid of the dogs alone
will be enough.

206
00:13:32,155 --> 00:13:34,366
[student 3] It'll be nice
to walk the hallways in peace.

207
00:13:34,449 --> 00:13:36,701
[student 4] Frankly,
separate education is a relief.

208
00:13:36,785 --> 00:13:39,079
Well, that's more weight
off our shoulders.

209
00:13:39,162 --> 00:13:40,956
- [indistinct chatter]
- I guess so.

210
00:13:41,039 --> 00:13:42,582
[Gon] As our last order of business,

211
00:13:42,666 --> 00:13:46,169
I would like to announce the students
for this year's Advanced Class.

212
00:13:46,253 --> 00:13:47,712
[student 1] Gonna the canines again.

213
00:13:47,796 --> 00:13:50,298
- [student 2] For sure.
- Please stand up if your name is called.

214
00:13:51,049 --> 00:13:52,592
Class A. Lando.

215
00:13:54,844 --> 00:13:56,304
Class C. Danny.

216
00:13:58,390 --> 00:13:59,849
Class E. Jack.

217
00:14:01,184 --> 00:14:02,143
[all] Oh!

218
00:14:02,227 --> 00:14:04,020
- [Gon] Class F. Lance.
- Whoo-hoo!

219
00:14:04,771 --> 00:14:06,523
[Gon] And Class G. Mick.

220
00:14:07,649 --> 00:14:09,651
That concludes our presentation.

221
00:14:10,777 --> 00:14:11,945
[popping]

222
00:14:12,028 --> 00:14:14,322
[all] Congratulations, Jack!

223
00:14:14,406 --> 00:14:16,199
[chuckles softly] Thanks, you guys.

224
00:14:16,283 --> 00:14:18,743
Our little boy is growing up so fast!

225
00:14:18,827 --> 00:14:21,913
Legoshi's tail is going to go berserk
when he finds out.

226
00:14:21,997 --> 00:14:24,040
[all laughing]

227
00:14:24,124 --> 00:14:27,127
- [cell phone buzzing]
- Ah. Excuse me a second.

228
00:14:28,461 --> 00:14:29,379
Hmm?

229
00:14:31,423 --> 00:14:32,340
This is Jack.

230
00:14:32,424 --> 00:14:36,094
[Gosha over phone] <i>Ah, Jack!
Do you know where Legoshi is?</i>

231
00:14:37,053 --> 00:14:39,806
Who is-- Oh, is this
Legoshi's grandfather?

232
00:14:40,515 --> 00:14:42,517
- Hey, sir, it's been ages!
- Legoshi's grandfather?

233
00:14:42,601 --> 00:14:45,270
[Gosha] <i>Is it true that Legoshi
dropped out of school?</i>

234
00:14:45,353 --> 00:14:47,814
<i>His tuition was refunded, and, well...</i>

235
00:14:47,898 --> 00:14:50,108
<i>I can't seem to get him
on the phone, either.</i>

236
00:14:50,191 --> 00:14:51,943
<i>Do you know anything about this?</i>

237
00:14:52,027 --> 00:14:54,487
I know he canceled his phone service,

238
00:14:54,571 --> 00:14:57,282
but I thought he'd already told you
he dropped out.

239
00:14:57,908 --> 00:14:58,742
GRADUATION

240
00:14:58,825 --> 00:15:01,620
[Gosha sighs] Sorry to get all worked up.
I'm just worried about him.

241
00:15:01,703 --> 00:15:05,749
{\an8}[Jack] <i>Sir, please don't worry.
Legoshi knows what he's doing.</i>

242
00:15:05,832 --> 00:15:06,791
{\an8}[Gosha] Yeah, but--

243
00:15:06,875 --> 00:15:09,210
{\an8}[Jack] <i>I'm sure he had a good reason
for dropping out.</i>

244
00:15:09,294 --> 00:15:12,172
{\an8}<i>He wouldn't have done it
if it wasn't right for him.</i>

245
00:15:12,255 --> 00:15:14,090
<i>He's the kind of guy you can trust.</i>

246
00:15:14,883 --> 00:15:19,304
[Gosha] I know. But after all,
the kid is my one and only grandchild.

247
00:15:25,685 --> 00:15:27,228
[Lisa panting]

248
00:15:28,855 --> 00:15:30,523
[Lisa] Ah, Haru! Hi!

249
00:15:30,607 --> 00:15:31,900
[Haru] Hey! Come, sit.

250
00:15:31,983 --> 00:15:33,485
[Lisa] Sorry we're late.

251
00:15:33,568 --> 00:15:36,488
Orientation for the new students
dragged on forever.

252
00:15:37,197 --> 00:15:38,865
- This is so great!
- Yeah.

253
00:15:38,949 --> 00:15:42,369
- I'd been wanting to check this place out.
- They make an incredible latte here.

254
00:15:42,452 --> 00:15:44,412
- That's exactly what I ordered.
- Really?

255
00:15:44,496 --> 00:15:45,914
I have to get one next time.

256
00:15:45,997 --> 00:15:49,167
- How was your course registration?
- Meh, I just chose whatever.

257
00:15:49,250 --> 00:15:52,879
My first year of university is off
to such a fantastic start.

258
00:15:52,963 --> 00:15:55,924
I've decided I want to make campus life
very exciting.

259
00:15:56,007 --> 00:15:59,344
It's the perfect way to say goodbye
to the bullied high-school-kid life.

260
00:15:59,886 --> 00:16:02,013
Hey, girls, guess what?

261
00:16:02,097 --> 00:16:05,058
I wanted you to meet my new boyfriend,
so I invited him to join us.

262
00:16:05,141 --> 00:16:06,351
- What?
- Huh?

263
00:16:06,434 --> 00:16:09,896
You seriously got yourself
a man already? No way!

264
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,315
- Haru, did you know?
- Huh? Oh. No.

265
00:16:12,399 --> 00:16:15,026
- So, what's he like?
- [Ako gasps] Here he comes now.

266
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:16,695
Wait-- Babe, over here!

267
00:16:18,113 --> 00:16:19,906
- [both gasp]
- [heavy footsteps approaching]

268
00:16:19,990 --> 00:16:20,824
[Lisa] Oh.

269
00:16:21,408 --> 00:16:24,995
[grunts] Hey, ladies. The name's Eado, yo.

270
00:16:25,078 --> 00:16:27,205
Ta-da! Meet my new baby boy.

271
00:16:27,831 --> 00:16:29,457
[both gasping]

272
00:16:29,541 --> 00:16:30,875
[Ako laughs]

273
00:16:31,626 --> 00:16:34,004
That's pretty much
exactly how I thought you'd react.

274
00:16:34,087 --> 00:16:35,296
Bit of a shock, huh?

275
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:39,175
Yeah, going out with Ako, we tend
to get that a lot around here. [chuckles]

276
00:16:39,259 --> 00:16:41,720
- [Ako] Mmm-hmm.
- [sheep scoffs] Do you smell that?

277
00:16:41,803 --> 00:16:44,639
- [sheep 2] Smells like a carnivore.
- [Lisa] Wow, that's great!

278
00:16:44,723 --> 00:16:47,225
It's enough to make you lose
your appetite.

279
00:16:47,892 --> 00:16:49,477
Can you even imagine

280
00:16:49,561 --> 00:16:53,231
a boyfriend from another species
back when we were in school?

281
00:16:53,314 --> 00:16:56,651
They'd call you a sicko for that.
And, actually, they'd be right.

282
00:16:56,735 --> 00:16:59,070
Staying with your own kind
is so much safer.

283
00:16:59,154 --> 00:17:00,864
I just hope she figures that out.

284
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,575
Come on, let's get out of here.

285
00:17:03,658 --> 00:17:05,201
[sheep 2 sighs] Good idea.

286
00:17:05,285 --> 00:17:09,122
[sighs] And we were having
such a good time just now.

287
00:17:09,789 --> 00:17:11,207
[sheep 1 sighs] What a shame.

288
00:17:11,291 --> 00:17:12,792
- [Eado sighs]
- [sheep 2] Where to?

289
00:17:12,876 --> 00:17:14,586
- [sheep 1] Uh, anywhere?
- [sheep 2] Like...

290
00:17:14,669 --> 00:17:15,503
[Ako, Eado sigh]

291
00:17:15,587 --> 00:17:17,047
[Haru] <i>Oh, Legoshi,</i>

292
00:17:17,630 --> 00:17:20,925
<i>turns out the real world is
a lot more complicated than I thought.</i>

293
00:17:21,009 --> 00:17:23,970
COEXISTENCE THEORY: THE BASICS
VEGETABLE NUTRITION

294
00:17:24,054 --> 00:17:27,390
[horn sounding]

295
00:17:27,474 --> 00:17:30,060
[rhythmic drumming]

296
00:17:30,143 --> 00:17:32,062
[festive music playing]

297
00:17:51,247 --> 00:17:53,249
[muffled playing continues]

298
00:17:55,251 --> 00:17:57,587
Young folks probably don't even know,

299
00:17:58,296 --> 00:17:59,214
but way back when,

300
00:17:59,297 --> 00:18:02,592
we had all sorts of events like this
that we'd be excited for.

301
00:18:03,676 --> 00:18:06,179
I still remember it all
like it was yesterday.

302
00:18:07,388 --> 00:18:12,936
Originally, this was a day that we had
to celebrate precious meat, to cherish it.

303
00:18:13,019 --> 00:18:14,979
That's why it's called Meat-Loving Day.

304
00:18:15,855 --> 00:18:17,732
And now, it's nothing but a day

305
00:18:17,816 --> 00:18:20,110
to kick off turf wars
across the Black Market.

306
00:18:23,404 --> 00:18:26,116
<i>Between the Komodo dragons' Doku-Gumi...</i>

307
00:18:26,199 --> 00:18:28,118
[muffled whooping, cheering]

308
00:18:28,201 --> 00:18:29,994
[Saiga] <i>...the red foxes' Inari-Gumi,</i>

309
00:18:31,496 --> 00:18:33,248
<i>the leopards' Madara-Gumi,</i>

310
00:18:34,249 --> 00:18:36,042
<i>and the lions' Shishi-Gumi.</i>

311
00:18:36,126 --> 00:18:38,628
[whooping, cheering continue]

312
00:18:38,711 --> 00:18:41,923
[Saiga] <i>That gang was thriving beautifully
until last year,</i>

313
00:18:42,549 --> 00:18:44,592
<i>but they've been slipping lately.</i>

314
00:18:46,469 --> 00:18:47,929
They don't have a boss now.

315
00:18:48,012 --> 00:18:50,348
And you can't call yourself
a gang without one.

316
00:18:51,432 --> 00:18:54,853
Anyway, it's Meat-Loving Day,
so I'm slashing prices.

317
00:18:55,520 --> 00:18:58,064
If it's possible,
do try to only take one bite.

318
00:18:58,815 --> 00:18:59,732
[sniffs]

319
00:19:00,483 --> 00:19:03,069
{\an8}Hang on, you're not a carnivore, are you--

320
00:19:03,153 --> 00:19:04,737
{\an8}[grunts, groans]

321
00:19:05,405 --> 00:19:07,407
[ominous music playing]

322
00:19:22,630 --> 00:19:25,800
[Legoshi retching]

323
00:19:28,094 --> 00:19:31,097
{\an8}- [Legoshi groaning, whimpering]
- [thudding, rumbling]

324
00:19:34,642 --> 00:19:38,021
[groans in frustration] That's enough!

325
00:19:38,104 --> 00:19:40,398
I'm going to deal with this
once and for all.

326
00:19:41,482 --> 00:19:43,610
[Legoshi continues groaning]

327
00:19:48,156 --> 00:19:49,157
[knocks on door]

328
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:51,784
- [Legoshi coughing]
- [opens door]

329
00:19:51,868 --> 00:19:54,454
Huh? Well, that's not very safe.

330
00:19:54,537 --> 00:19:56,748
- [door creaking]
- [Legoshi breathing heavily]

331
00:19:58,499 --> 00:20:00,043
[suspenseful music playing]

332
00:20:01,294 --> 00:20:02,712
[heavy breathing continues]

333
00:20:03,379 --> 00:20:05,381
[low growling]

334
00:20:06,007 --> 00:20:07,050
Excuse me...

335
00:20:09,552 --> 00:20:10,511
Are you okay?

336
00:20:11,012 --> 00:20:12,430
[yelping]

337
00:20:12,513 --> 00:20:14,933
- [growls]
- [shuddering]

338
00:20:15,767 --> 00:20:17,810
[growling]

339
00:20:20,104 --> 00:20:21,773
[grinding]

340
00:20:23,816 --> 00:20:27,737
[Agata] Seriously? You can't give us
even a little more time?

341
00:20:27,820 --> 00:20:30,281
'Fraid not. You know full well
what the deal is.

342
00:20:30,365 --> 00:20:32,742
If you don't bring the ingredients,
I can't make the drugs.

343
00:20:32,825 --> 00:20:36,788
But we've been super busy lately.
We don't have time for that.

344
00:20:36,871 --> 00:20:39,666
Busy doing what?
Eating your pretty boy boss?

345
00:20:39,749 --> 00:20:41,000
- What?
- [both growl]

346
00:20:41,084 --> 00:20:43,586
You realize this is your problem
more than ours?

347
00:20:44,337 --> 00:20:47,548
You cats aren't the be-all-end-all
of the Hyperdrug.

348
00:20:47,632 --> 00:20:49,467
I'm sure another gang would take the work.

349
00:20:49,550 --> 00:20:52,262
What if we can figure out something
by next week, huh?

350
00:20:52,345 --> 00:20:54,722
[scoffs] Talk about unreliable!

351
00:20:55,598 --> 00:20:58,309
If you can't even come up
with a single piece of ivory,

352
00:20:58,393 --> 00:21:00,561
that doesn't bode well
for our relationship.

353
00:21:00,645 --> 00:21:02,272
- [Melon sighs]
- [thuds]

354
00:21:02,355 --> 00:21:05,400
- Oh?
- [Melon] Sorry for the wait. How's this?

355
00:21:09,028 --> 00:21:11,489
Oh. [chuckles excitedly]

356
00:21:11,572 --> 00:21:14,367
The renowned Shishi-Gumi
comes through again!

357
00:21:14,450 --> 00:21:16,828
Such gorgeous high-quality ivory!

358
00:21:17,495 --> 00:21:19,372
Yo, who is that?

359
00:21:19,455 --> 00:21:20,290
I don't know.

360
00:21:21,207 --> 00:21:23,710
[Melon] I take it
you can make the drug now? Right?

361
00:21:24,544 --> 00:21:27,380
- Don't miss the deadline.
- Uh, yes, sir!

362
00:21:27,964 --> 00:21:29,215
Don't boss us around.

363
00:21:29,299 --> 00:21:31,342
You're the ones
who almost missed the delivery.

364
00:21:32,176 --> 00:21:35,722
[Melon inhales, sighs heavily]

365
00:21:35,805 --> 00:21:38,224
[puffing playfully]

366
00:21:38,308 --> 00:21:39,225
Uh...

367
00:21:40,018 --> 00:21:41,561
[nervously] Uh... Uh...

368
00:21:41,644 --> 00:21:44,147
- [whimpers]
- [Melon sighs, grunts]

369
00:21:44,230 --> 00:21:47,859
Punk! What do you think
you're doing-- [groans]

370
00:21:49,068 --> 00:21:51,487
[Melon sighs] Silly cat,
let's get this straight.

371
00:21:51,988 --> 00:21:52,947
[Dolph, Agata gasp]

372
00:21:53,031 --> 00:21:55,742
[Melon] That's really no way
to talk to your <i>boss...</i>

373
00:21:55,825 --> 00:21:57,785
- Now is it?
- [Free groans softly]

374
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

375
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,834
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

376
00:22:04,917 --> 00:22:08,338
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

377
00:22:09,422 --> 00:22:12,508
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

378
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,845
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

379
00:22:17,805 --> 00:22:21,017
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

380
00:22:21,100 --> 00:22:23,603
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

381
00:22:23,686 --> 00:22:26,314
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

382
00:22:27,648 --> 00:22:31,611
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

383
00:22:32,612 --> 00:22:37,075
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

384
00:22:37,158 --> 00:22:40,078
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

385
00:22:40,161 --> 00:22:44,749
<i>- ♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

386
00:22:44,832 --> 00:22:46,834
<i>- ♪ Till I... ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

387
00:22:46,918 --> 00:22:48,002
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

388
00:22:48,086 --> 00:22:52,590
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

389
00:22:53,341 --> 00:22:56,552
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

390
00:22:56,636 --> 00:23:00,848
<i>- ♪ Just want to feel like this ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

391
00:23:00,932 --> 00:23:02,725
<i>- ♪ Till the... ♪
- ♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

392
00:23:02,809 --> 00:23:04,102
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

393
00:23:04,894 --> 00:23:08,856
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my side ♪</i>

394
00:23:09,398 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

395
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,735
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

396
00:23:13,444 --> 00:23:16,239
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

397
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

398
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,497
<i>- ♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪
- ♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

399
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:29,127
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪
- ♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
